.TH MAIL 1 "2026-09-22" "Mailhub 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mail \- Mailhub user CLI (thin REST client)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mail
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fICOMMAND\fR [\fIARGS\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mail
is a thin HTTP client for the Mailhub REST API. It communicates with the
local \fBmailhub serve\fR daemon (default: http://127.0.0.1:8787) to
search, read, send, and draft messages across configured accounts.
.PP
All commands require a running Mailhub server. The CLI uses bearer tokens
stored by \fBmailhub init\fR and \fBmailhub serve\fR for authentication.
.PP
Message bodies are treated as untrusted input. Message IDs are opaque and
must not be cached across sessions.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB--url\fR \fIURL\fR
Mailhub server URL (default: http://127.0.0.1:8787). Must use loopback
address (127.0.0.1, localhost, or ::1).
.TP
\fB--token\fR \fITOKEN\fR
Explicit bearer token to use for authentication.
.TP
\fB--ro\fR
Use read-only token (default uses full-access token).
.TP
\fB--json\fR
Output JSON instead of formatted text.
.TP
\fB--confirm\fR
Confirm sending a message (required for \fBsend\fR command).
.TP
\fB--config\fR \fIPATH\fR
Configuration file path (default: ~/.config/mailhub/config.toml).
.TP
\fB--state\fR \fIPATH\fR
Credential state file path (default: ~/.local/state/mailhub/credentials.json).
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
\fBaccounts\fR
List configured accounts with their providers and capabilities.
.TP
\fBfolders\fR \fIACCOUNT\fR
List folders (IMAP) or labels (Gmail) for \fIACCOUNT\fR.
.TP
\fBsearch\fR \fIACCOUNT\fR \fIQUERY\fR [\fB--max-results\fR \fIN\fR] [\fB--page-token\fR \fITOKEN\fR]
Search messages in \fIACCOUNT\fR using provider-specific query syntax.
Gmail uses Gmail search operators; Graph uses OData filter/KQL.
.TP
\fBget\fR \fIACCOUNT\fR \fIMESSAGE_ID\fR
Get a message by its opaque ID. Returns full message with headers and body.
.TP
\fBsend\fR \fIACCOUNT\fR \fB--to\fR \fIEMAIL\fR [\fB--cc\fR \fIEMAIL\fR] [\fB--bcc\fR \fIEMAIL\fR] \fB--subject\fR \fISUBJECT\fR [\fB--text-body\fR \fITEXT\fR] [\fB--html-body\fR \fIHTML\fR] [\fB--html\fR] [\fB--body-file\fR \fIFILE\fR] [\fB--in-reply-to\fR \fIID\fR] [\fB--references\fR \fIID\fR...] \fB--confirm\fR
Send a message. Requires \fB--confirm\fR flag. Recipients must be on the
account's allowlist unless \fBallow_anywhere = true\fR in config.
Body can be provided via \fB--text-body\fR, \fB--html-body\fR, or
\fB--body-file\fR (with \fB--html\fR to treat as HTML).
.TP
\fBdraft\fR \fIACCOUNT\fR \fB--to\fR \fIEMAIL\fR [\fB--cc\fR \fIEMAIL\fR] [\fB--bcc\fR \fIEMAIL\fR] \fB--subject\fR \fISUBJECT\fR [\fB--text-body\fR \fITEXT\fR] [\fB--html-body\fR \fIHTML\fR] [\fB--html\fR] [\fB--body-file\fR \fIFILE\fR] [\fB--in-reply-to\fR \fIID\fR] [\fB--references\fR \fIID\fR...]
Create a draft message. Same body options as \fBsend\fR but no confirmation
required.
.SH FILES
.TP
\fI~/.config/mailhub/config.toml\fR
Account definitions and allowlists.
.TP
\fI~/.local/state/mailhub/credentials.json\fR
Bearer tokens for authentication.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
List accounts and search for unread messages:
.B mail accounts
.br
.B mail search personal "is:unread"
.br
.B mail search work "from:boss@example.com"
.TP
Read a message and send a reply:
.B mail get personal MSG123
.br
.B mail send personal --to sender@example.com --subject "Re: Hello" --text-body "Thanks!" --in-reply-to MSG123 --confirm
.TP
Create a draft with HTML body from file:
.B mail draft personal --to team@example.com --subject "Update" --body-file update.html --html
.TP
Use read-only token for searching:
.B mail --ro search personal "newer_than:7d"
.TP
Output as JSON for scripting:
.B mail --json folders personal
